spans.s:
‘impulse’, motive, cause, cause of, reason for (loc., rarely dat. or gen.;
हेतुना, हेतोः, हेतवे, हेतौ, ‘for a cause or reason’, ‘by reason of’, ‘on account of’ [with gen. or comp., e.g. मम हेतोः or मद्-धेतोः, ‘on account of me’];
कं हेतुम् or को हेतुः, ‘wherefore?’ ‘why?’, Pāṇ. ii, 2, 23;
Pat.;
यतो हेतोः, ‘because’;
अनेन हेतुना or

, ‘for this reason’;
मृत्यु-हेतवे, ‘in order to kill’;
हेतुर् अलौकिकः, ‘a supernatural cause’;
ifc. हेतु also = ‘having as a cause or motive’, ‘caused or effected or actuated or attracted or impelled by’ e.g. कर्म-हेतु, ‘caused by the acts [of a former existence]’, Mn. i, 49;
मांस-हेतु, ‘attracted by [the smell of] flesh’, MBh. x, 496;
कर्म-फल-हेतु, ‘impelled by [the expectation of] the consequences of any act’, BhP. ii, 47; 49), RV. &c. &c.
